🌐 HTTP (HyperText Transfer Protocol)
1.Data is sent in plain text
2.Not secure
3.Anyone can read the data

Example:
http://example.com

📌 Risk:
Passwords, messages, or details can be stolen ❌


🔒 HTTPS (HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure)
1.Data is encrypted
2.Secure
3.Uses SSL/TLS certificate

Example:
https://example.com

📌 Safe:
Even if someone intercepts data, they can’t read it 


✅ One-line summary
HTTP = unsafe communication
HTTPS = secure communication using encryption